      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Mau Mau Uprising (1952-1960) was a crucial struggle for Kenyan independence, led by the Mau Mau fighters, primarily from the Kikuyu ethnic group. The uprising began in 1952, when the Mau Mau, frustrated by British colonial rule and land dispossession, launched an armed rebellion. The British response was brutal, involving mass arrests, torture, and concentration camps, which only fueled the resistance. Key events include the declaration of the Mau Mau oath in 1952, the Battle of Ngong Hills in 1954, and the eventual British crackdown in 1956. The uprising culminated in 1960 with the signing of the independence agreement, leading to Kenya's independence in 1963. The Mau Mau fighters are celebrated as heroes in Kenya for their relentless fight against colonial oppression.",
